  countsTowardMapAchievements: 1
  isStoryModeContract: 1
  isTutorialContract: 0
  autoCollectReward: 0
  featureUnlockRewards: []
  clientName: Silas
  jobDescription: We need a bridge across this ravine!
  budget: 200000
  liveLoadWeight: 1000
  bridgeSpan: 30
  allowedMaterials: []
  hiddenTools: 
  hiddenMaterials: []
  enforceMaxStress: 0
  maxAllowedStress: 100
  isTimeAttack: 0
  timeAttackDuration: 60
  winCondition: 0
  requiredIntactTime: 5
  goldReward: 500
  expReward: 100
  offerDialogue:
    name: Silas
    sentences:
    - This is a wider crossing than the ones you've handled before.
    - There is a rock formation partway across, but it sits much lower than the roads
      on either side.
    - <b><#E09500>You'll have to decide how to use the available support points across
      the site</color></b>.
    - The test jeep will place weight on different parts of the bridge as it moves.
    - <b><#E09500>Watch how that load is distributed across the whole structure</color></b>.
    - If your bridge carries the jeep safely, Vance's supplies can then reach the
      community by this route.
    - If you're ready, take the contract.
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Silas
    sentences: []
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Silas
    sentences:
    - Vance's shipment has already made it halfway.
    - This bridge is the final connection to the community.
    - Do not rush the design. Watch how the jeep's weight spreads through
      the structure as it crosses.
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Silas
    sentences:
    - The final crossing is open.
    - Vance's factory is now connected to the middle ravine, and this bridge carries
      the route the rest of the way to the community.
    - They will not have to wait for deliveries to travel all the way around the
      canyon anymore.
    - What started as one shipment is now a complete supply route.
    - This crossing was wider than your earlier projects, and the test jeep placed
      weight across the entire structure.
    - You handled the load distribution well.
    - Good work, {PlayerName}.
    - Stay nearby. There is another passage farther east that we still need to discuss.
